SYNTHESIS
  The carrier-product comparison is naturally a miss-zeta statement:
    product cover - actual p0 = sum_R (-1)^|R|(z_product(R)-z_actual(R)).
  Important correction: in this anchor-separated gauge, ProductCover is
  not an upper bound in the tested rows; actual p0 can exceed the product.
  The needed lemma is the symmetric budget statement
    |actual - product| <= cap_k - product,
  and the tested ratios are small relative to that budget.
  The useful proof currency is residual-size layers, not raw pointwise
  residual-coordinate dominance.  This avoids the false small-R cone route
  while preserving the exact product structure Route E needs.
  Boolean-cube reading: the same error is the h=6 Krawtchouk/MacWilliams
  coordinate M_6 of the radial miss-zeta discrepancy.  The proof target
  should bound this signed top character after routing low-height
  resonances, not the full residual-coordinate L1 norm.
  Next target: prove a signed Erdos-Turan/Koksma bound for the zeta layers
  whose unsigned mass is large, and use the product cap slack for the rest.
